---
import Public from '../layouts/Public.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import homeImage from '../assets/img/home.jpeg';
---

<Public pageTitle="Home Page">
	<div class="flex justify-around w-4xl mx-auto text-xl">
		<article class="w-xl">
			<div class="mb-4">
				<h2 class="text-2xl">This is a blog</h2>
				<p>
					I write some stuff here, feel free to read it.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="mb-4">
				<h2 class="text-2xl">Maybe not?</h2>
				<p>Super social links and stuff</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Github</li>
					<li>Email</li>
					<li>Curriculum</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div class="mb-4">
				<h2 class="text-2xl">Tech used here</h2>
				<p>
					I went through lots and lots of different iterations of this blog. The original one was made with the <a href="https://django.com">Django</a> framework, a shame i lost the SSH key of the Oracle instance that was running it. So, the missing SSH key and the different stuff that i was studying at the time made me feel the desire to make a new blog, it just took me... 6 months to decide how i wanted to do it. So... the stack is... <a href="#">Astro</a> framework and <a href="#">Tailwind</a>, just that. I will explain better the decisions in a post.
				</p>
			</div>
		</article>
		<section>
			<Image src={homeImage} alt="Super cool image of the Schrodinger Cat" width="340" height="540"/>
		</section>
	</div>
</Public>
